Dedication — in honor of Robert J. Shiller (Yale; Nobel 2013), whose work on
narratives, animal spirits, irrational exuberance, and the phishing equilibrium
taught a generation to tell a story backed by cash flow from a story backed by
nothing. And to George A. Akerlof, co-author of *Animal Spirits* and *Phishing
for Phools*, from whose preface this skill takes its conscience:

  "We wrote this book as admirers of the free market system, but hoping to help
   people better find their way in it. ... We all have to navigate this system in
   order to maintain our dignity and integrity."

Build on the right side of the pun.
